\subsection{\code{BaseRCdplotLayerProcessor$generate_selectors()}}{
  Address each band by the polygon that drew it

\code{cdplot()} writes one \code{polygon} grob per band, in draw order, which
is the bottom-to-top order the series are in. The frame it draws
around the plot is a polygon too, but gridGraphics names it
\code{-box-1} rather than \code{-polygon-N}, so the anchored pattern does not
collect it.

Withheld entirely when the counts disagree, for the reason every
processor here gives: a partial list hands a band its neighbour's
element, and a user cannot tell that apart from a correct one.
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{BaseRCdplotLayerProcessor$generate_selectors(
  layer_info,
  gt = NULL,
  n_series = 0L
)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Arguments}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
    \describe{
      \item{\code{layer_info}}{The recorded call}
      \item{\code{gt}}{The grob tree}
      \item{\code{n_series}}{How many bands the data reports}
    }
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Returns}{
    A list of CSS selectors, one per band
  }
}

